# Marketplace: Location API (`y-mp-location`)

Use this rule for **Location** operations on **Marketplace testing** via HTTP—especially **`LOCATION` → `locationId`** for **`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-work-order.mdc`** and scripts. Resolve **`CLIENT` → `CLIENT_ID`** first when needed via **`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-client.mdc`**.

Any saved responses, debug JSON, or scratch files: **`cursor_workspace/`** per **y-mp-ai-temp**.

## Configuration

Load secrets and URLs **only** from:

``.env.e2e.local` (repo root)`

- **`MARKETPLACE_JWT`**, **`MARKETPLACE_URL`**, **`VENDOROO_BASE_API_URL`** (optional), **`CLIENT_ID`**, **`LOCATION`** (human label / unit name from MP).
- **Headers** on every call: `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`, **`User-Agent`** (desktop Chrome string), **`Origin`** + **`Referer`** = **`MARKETPLACE_URL`** (without trailing issues—trim slash if needed). Testing MP often **403** without **`User-Agent`**.

**OpenAPI:** [https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai/swagger/v1/swagger.json](https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai/swagger/v1/swagger.json) — tag **Location**, schemas **`LocationCreateDto`**, **`LocationDetailDto`**, **`LocationSearchResultDtoPaginatedListApiResult`**, etc.

---

## Read / search

### 1) Search by free text (best for `LOCATION` in `.env.e2e.local`)

**`GET {api}/api/Location/SearchLocations`**

| Query param | Notes |
|-------------|--------|
| **`SearchText`** | Required for label search — use the same string as **`LOCATION`** (URL-encoded). |
| **`ClientId`** | Set to **`CLIENT_ID`** to scope to that client. |
| **`PageSize`** | e.g. `20` (optional but recommended). |
| **`PageNumber`** | **Use `1` for the first page.** On testing MP, **`PageNumber=0` triggers HTTP 500**. Omitting **`PageNumber`** and sending only **`SearchText`**, **`ClientId`**, and **`PageSize`** also works. |

Parse **`data.items`** (or PascalCase equivalents): each hit includes **`id`**, **`name`**, **`address`**, etc. Pick the row whose **`name`** **exactly equals** **`LOCATION`** if possible; otherwise the closest single match and confirm with the user.

**Example (placeholders only):**

```text
GET {api}/api/Location/SearchLocations?SearchText=Yaser%20LOC%201&ClientId=198&PageNumber=1&PageSize=20
```

### 2) List all locations for a client (fallback + disambiguation)

**`GET {api}/api/Location/GetByClientId?clientId={CLIENT_ID}`**

Returns **`data`**: array of **`LocationDetailDto`**. Client-side filter:

- **Exact:** `loc.name.strip().lower() == LOCATION.strip().lower()`
- **Substring:** `LOCATION.lower() in (name + " " + address).lower()` if labels are messy

Use this when **`SearchLocations`** is empty, returns multiple ambiguous rows, or errors.

### 3) Other reads (optional)

- **`GET {api}/api/Location`** — list-shaped response in OpenAPI; behavior depends on auth context—prefer **`GetByClientId`** / **`SearchLocations`** for automation.
- **`GET {api}/api/Location/History/{locationId}`**, **`GET …/Notes/{locationId}`**, **`GET …/GetPOCByLocationId/{locationId}`** — audit / notes / POC (see Swagger).

---

## Create

**`POST {api}/api/Location`**  
**Body:** JSON **`LocationCreateDto`** (`application/json` or OData content-type variants Swagger lists).

Typical fields: **`clientId`**, **`name`**, **`haveAddress`**, **`address`**, **`city`**, **`state`**, **`zipCode`**, **`country`**, coordinates, **`data`**, etc. Follow **`LocationCreateDto`** for required combinations in your environment.

**Response:** **`LocationDetailDtoApiResult`** — use returned **`data.id`** as the new **`locationId`**.

---

## Update

**`PUT {api}/api/Location?id={locationId}`**  
**Body:** JSON **`LocationCreateDto`** (same schema as create; include **`id`** in body if required by your build—see Swagger).

---

## Delete

**`DELETE {api}/api/Location/{id}`**  
**Path:** integer location **`id`**. Returns generic **`ApiResult`**. Prefer soft-delete semantics if your org discourages hard deletes—confirm with the team before automating deletes.

---

## Related endpoints (not full CRUD on the row)

Use Swagger when you need:

- **`POST /api/Location/AssignUser`**, **`POST /api/Location/BulkUpdate`**, **`PATCH /api/Location/BatchUpdate/{id}`**
- **`POST/PUT/DELETE` `…/LocationPolicy`** and **`…/LocationPolicy/Assignment`**
- **`POST /api/Location/{id}/AddDocument`**, **`DELETE …/DeleteDocument/…`**
- **`POST /api/Location/GetWithPagination`** — advanced list (needs **`LocationSearchDtoPaginationRequest`**; easy to misconfigure—prefer **`SearchLocations`** + **`GetByClientId`** for agents)

---

## Linking to work orders

After resolving **`locationId`** from **`LOCATION`**, pass it to **`POST /api/WorkOrder`** (multipart `WorkOrder` JSON) per **`.cursor/rules/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-work-order.mdc`**. Optionally store **`MARKETPLACE_LOCATION_ID=<id>`** in **`.env.e2e.local`** to skip lookup on repeat runs (do not commit secrets).

---

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Action |
|--------|--------|
| **403** on API | Add **`User-Agent`**, **`Origin`**, **`Referer`**; refresh JWT. |
| **500** on **`SearchLocations`** with pagination | Avoid **`PageNumber=0`**; use **`PageNumber=1`** or omit **`PageNumber`**. |
| No hits | **`GetByClientId`** + manual filter; verify **`CLIENT_ID`** matches the client that owns the location. |
| Multiple matches | Prefer **exact `name` == `LOCATION`**; else ask the user which **`id`**. |
